  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "What is the sum of the digits of the decimal form of the product \\(2^{1999} \\cdot 5^{2001}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(7\\)",
    "E": "\\(10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each factor \\(2\\) can pair with a factor \\(5\\) to make \\(10\\). There are \\(1999\\) such pairs, leaving \\(2001-1999=2\\) factors of \\(5\\). Therefore\n\\[\n2^{1999}\\cdot5^{2001}\n=(2\\cdot5)^{1999}\\cdot5^2\n=25\\cdot10^{1999}.\n\\]\nMultiplication by \\(10^{1999}\\) appends \\(1999\\) zeros to \\(25\\). Those zeros contribute nothing to the digit sum, so the sum is \\(2+5=7\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
